===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|act of entering}} The act of [[enter]]ing.
#: {{ux|en|The wrestler's dramatic '''entry''' into the stadium was very impressive.}}
# {{senseid|en|permission to enter}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} Permission to enter.
#: {{ux|en|Children are allowed '''entry''' only if accompanied by an adult.}}
#: {{ux|en|Strictly no '''entry''' for under-18s}}
# {{senseid|en|entryway such as a doorway}} A [[doorway]] that provides a means of entering a building.
# {{lb|en|legal}} The act of taking [[possession]].
#: {{rfex|en}}
# {{senseid|en|start of an insurance contract}} {{lb|en|insurance}} The start of an [[insurance]] contract.
# {{senseid|en|passageway between terraced houses}} {{lb|en|Midlands}} A [[passageway]] between [[terraced]] houses that provides a means of entering a back [[garden]] or [[yard]].
# {{senseid|en|entryway such as a foyer}} A small [[room]] immediately inside the front door of a house or other building, often having an access to a [[stairway]] and leading on to other rooms.
# {{senseid|en|church group for fellowship}} A small group formed within a church, especially [[Episcopal]], for simple dinner and fellowship, and to help facilitate new friendships.
# {{senseid|en|item in a list, such as a headword}} An [[item]] in a [[list]], such as an [[article]] in a [[dictionary]] or [[encyclopedia]].
#: {{mer|en|headword<qq:sometimes synonymous>}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''entry''' on spiders is on page number 69.}}
# {{senseid|en|record in a log, diary, or database}} A [[record]] made in a [[log]], [[diary]] or anything similarly organized; {{lb|en|computing}} a [[datum]] in a database.
#: {{ux|en|What does the '''entry''' for 2 August 2005 say?}}
# {{senseid|en|algebraic term at any position in a matrix}} {{lb|en|linear algebra}} A [[term]] at any position in a [[matrix]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''entry''' in the second row and first column of this matrix is 6.}}
# {{senseid|en|report of ship to customs}} The exhibition or depositing of a ship's papers at the customhouse, to procure licence to land goods; or the giving an account of a ship's cargo to the officer of the customs, and obtaining his permission to land the goods.
# {{senseid|en|entrance of musician}} {{lb|en|music}} The point when a musician starts to play or sing; [[entrance]].
# {{senseid|en|introduction of new hounds into a pack}} {{lb|en|hunting}} The introduction of new hounds into a pack.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1956|title=Baily's Hunting Directory|page=311|text=Here was an excellent '''entry''' of hounds which would have fulfilled the late Earl Bathurst's dictum that breeders should always breed from hounds rather larger than those which they expect to put on.}}

